From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: gpiolib: do not warn about the static GPIO bases

Thingino addresses pins by the flat PA0..PE31 numbers in thingino.json,
the motors module and the boot scripts, so the Ingenic pinctrl driver
keeps the per-bank static bases. The deprecation warning is noise on
every boot; leave it at debug level.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpiolib.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpiolib.c
@@ -1277,8 +1277,8 @@
 			 */
 			gc->base = base;
 		} else {
-			dev_warn(&gdev->dev,
-				 "Static allocation of GPIO base is deprecated, use dynamic allocation.\n");
+			dev_dbg(&gdev->dev,
+				"Static allocation of GPIO base is deprecated, use dynamic allocation.\n");
 		}
 
 		gdev->base = base;
